 "context": [
  {
   "h": "Hannibal and Antiochus",
   "body": "<p>Antiochus III welcomed Hannibal in 195 BC. According to Livy, Hannibal urged him to carry the war to Italy, with Carthage brought in on his side, rather than fight Rome in Greece. Antiochus chose Greece: he landed there in 192 BC, was beaten by the Romans at Thermopylae in 191, and withdrew to Asia.</p><p>In 190 BC Hannibal commanded part of the king's fleet and was defeated by the Rhodians off Side in Pamphylia (the battle of the Eurymedon). Later that year, or early in 189, the Romans under Lucius Scipio crushed Antiochus' army at Magnesia. By the peace of Apamea (188 BC) Antiochus gave up his lands in Asia Minor and was required to hand Hannibal over to Rome.</p>"
  }
